* {{fr-IPA}}
* {{audio|Fr-dé.ogg|audio|lang=fr}}
* {{rhymes|e|lang=fr}}

===Etymology 1===
Obscure, perhaps from a {{inh|fr|VL.||*dadu}}, itself from {{der|fr|la|dātum}}, or alternatively of {{der|fr|ar|-}} origin; cf {{m|ar|أَعْدَاد}}. Compare Catalan {{m|ca|dau}}, Italian, Portuguese, and Spanish {{m|es|dado}}.

====Noun====
{{fr-noun|m}}

# [[die#Noun|die]] ([[dice]])
# [[diced]] slice (of meat)

===Etymology 2===
From an alteration of {{inh|fr|fro|deel}} (influenced by the above word), from {{inh|fr|LL.|digitāle}} < {{inh|fr|la|digitālis}}.

====Noun====
